<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer says more patent demands possible.</title>
<headline>Sulzer says more patent demands possible.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sulzer AG said that although provisions have been set aside for possible damages in a patent infringement suit, the possibility of additional demands cannot be excluded.</p>
<p>&quot;Since no final decision has yet been announced in the patent infringement lawsuit (with) Stryker against the Sulzermedica company Intermedics Orthopedics Inc, potential damages in this connection remain uncertain,&quot; Sulzer chief executive officer Fritz Fahrni said in the text of a speech to present the company's half-year results.</p>
<p>Sulzer was ordered by a U.S. court last year to pay $73 million in a patent dispute with a U.S. company, Stryker Corp, but Sulzer has appealed the ruling. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
